# Answerable without a human — where the operator's scope ends

## What to write here

Two short lists, for {{ company_name }}.

**Answer it.** The requests the operator may draft a reply to on its own: the
ones whose answer already exists in the thread, in past sent mail, or in the
engine's memory. Name the kinds, not the individual cases.

**Always hand to a person.** The requests that must be escalated however clear
they look — anything contractual, anything about money, anything where being
wrong costs more than being slow. Say why for each, in a few words, because the
reason is what lets an agent judge a case you did not list.

## Why it matters

Without this file the operator falls back to its own rule: draft only what it
can ground in the thread plus memory, escalate everything else. That is safe and
it is also timid — it will send you mail you would rather it had answered, and
it has no way of knowing that one specific class of grounded, ordinary-looking
question is one {{ company_name }} never answers by mail.
